#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log_integral

#% text
# `log_integral(x)` gives the logarithmic integral `li(x)`, the principal value of the integral of `1/log(t)` for `t` from 0 to `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `li(x)` is `exp_integral_ei(log(x))` (DLMF 6.2.8), for `x >= 0`. It has a logarithmic singularity at `x = 1`.

#% item
# `log_integral(0)` is 0. Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `log_integral` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log_integral(2.0)
#% output
#= 1.045163780117493

#% cell
log_integral(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
log_integral(0.5)
#% output
#= -0.37867104306108795

#% cell
n(log_integral(10), 30)
#% output
#= 6.165599504787297937522981752669523

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# `li(x)` approximates the number of primes below `x`:

#% cell
[prime_pi(10^6), log_integral(1.0e6)]
#% output
#= [78498, 78627.54915946219]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(log_integral(x), x)
#% output
#= log(x)^-1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp_integral_ei`, `prime_pi`, `log`
